{"skill":{"slug":"wonda","displayName":"Wonda"},"version":{"version":"1.2.0","createdAt":1776872244669,"changelog":"### Added\n- Local ffmpeg command routing — 8 new content skills for on-device video finishing (trims, captions, social reformat, scene splits, silence cuts, frame extraction, analysis artifacts) that keep bytes local instead of round-tripping through the API.\n- `remotion-local-render` — render editorPipeline blueprints locally via @remotion/renderer.\n- `tiktok-slideshow-carousel` — 3-slide hook/bridge/reveal carousel skill.\n- Social-signup primitive pattern — screenshot → decide → tap/type/swipe loop using `wonda device` + throwaway `wonda email` mailboxes for Instagram/TikTok flows.\n- `wonda device stream` — signed `playerUrl` (1h JWT) for handing control to a human on CAPTCHA screens or consent-gated steps.\n- Step 2.5 decision flow: when to finish locally vs remote.\n- ClawHub runtime metadata (requires.env, primaryEnv, npm + brew install specs) so security analysis matches what the skill actually references.\n\n### Changed\n- Install order: npm first, then Homebrew.\n- Auth simplified: `wonda auth login` or `WONDERCAT_API_KEY` env var.\n\n### Removed\n- `curl | bash` installer reference.\n- `WONDERCAT_BASE_URL`, `wonda config set api-key`, and cookie/session references.","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":51817,"sha256":"6a26d84fa894120b10b1bc51d1dd01750647bd2e4d15a3cb43810803e85ccab1","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2595,"sha256":"ce2bc6d0914124246fd475901f0086f9afc6ec70de388de0785891da3d7a2afc","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789537231084,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"ba6ec85d46fa903e14814335bb119cffb2270f16b9a6c9bae0dd4ce8980c6f86","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/ba6ec85d46fa903e14814335bb119cffb2270f16b9a6c9bae0dd4ce8980c6f86","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780090514632},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":90,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":11,"checkedAt":1789537231084},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill documents useful media workflows but also enables stealthy social-account automation and broad social posting or messaging authority.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The requested API key, connected social accounts, social auth tokens, private message access, hosted devices, and signed device-stream handoff URLs are high-impact capabilities that exceed simple media generation.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Install instructions use mutable global npm and Homebrew sources, and Patchright is installed unpinned with a runtime Chromium download for browser automation.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill instructs agents to fetch mutable remote Wonda content skills and execute each step, and it does not require explicit confirmation before every social write action such as tweets, replies, likes, follows, LinkedIn messages, Reddit DMs, or deletions.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No hidden system persistence or local backdoor was found, but the skill relies on persistent CLI installs, saved social credentials or tokens, and auto-refreshed Reddit chat tokens.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated Wonda media and social automation purpose is coherent, but the artifact goes beyond ordinary publishing by documenting throwaway-email social signups, hosted device control, internal X APIs, stealth browser modes, DMs, follows, deletes, and detection-avoidance tactics.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you intentionally want an agent to use Wonda with connected social accounts and you are prepared to review every external action. Avoid the documented stealth, disposable signup, internal API, and detection-avoidance workflows; prefer official account APIs, pinned dependencies, an isolated environment, and explicit confirmation before posting, messaging, following, deleting, or accepting terms.","findings":"[SDI-2] unexpected: Accepted in part: the stealth browser, internal API, secondary-account, throwaway signup, and detection-avoidance instructions are materially concerning even though social automation is disclosed.\n[T01] expected: Accepted as a Review concern: dynamic Wonda content skills fit the product workflow, but the instruction to fetch and execute remote steps lacks pinning, integrity checks, and explicit user approval.\n[T08] unexpected: Accepted: unpinned global package installs and unpinned Patchright browser setup create supply-chain risk for a skill handling authenticated media and social accounts.\n[other] unexpected: Accepted: artifact-backed evidence shows disposable-account creation, internal APIs, undetected browser automation, human-like delays, and rate limits framed as avoiding detection.\n[SDI-4] unexpected: Accepted: claims such as zero fingerprinting risk and fully safe understate the real platform, account, and compliance risk of stealth automation.\n[EA3] expected: Accepted as contextual: Reddit chat reads and DMs are disclosed social automation features, but they add to the high-impact account authority users should review.\n[P9] expected: Downgraded: manual inspection found the flagged whitespace was markdown table formatting, not concealed instructions.\n[EA2] expected: Downgraded: the cited automatic watermark-removal wording is a disclosed media-model behavior and not evidence of destructive local action.\n[SQP-1] expected: Downgraded: the broad description matches the broad CLI guide, though the breadth increases invocation and authority risk.\n[SQP-3] expected: Downgraded: the language guidance is a minor quality issue, not a material security concern.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789537231084}}}}}